<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31263" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσᾰκούω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hearken</i> or <i>give ear to</i> one, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς ἔφατ᾽:</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἐσάκουσε.. Ὀδυσσεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.97
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.133
			</span></i>, al. : c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωνὴν ἐσάκουσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Cer.</u>
					284
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				559
			</span></i>, etc. : c. gen. pers., <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				789
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἐμῶν λόγων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					1368
				</span></i>
			 : c. dat. pers., <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.214
			</span></i>, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					9.60
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>give way, yield</i> to a request, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.126
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				3.4
			</span></i>; of God, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινός</span> or 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς προσευχῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ps.</u>
					4.2
				</span></i>
			, etc. :—so in 
				Pass.
			, of the prayer, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				1.13
			</span></i> ; of the person, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				6.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in Poets,
			simply, <i>hear,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τούτου λέγοντος εἰσήκουσ᾽ ἐγώ, ὡς..</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					351
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίνος βροτῶν λόγον τόνδ᾽
			εἰ.</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>El.</u>
				884
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Aj.</u>
				318
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Axiop.
				1.12
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῶντ᾽ εἰσακούσας παῖδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					416
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>perceive, feel effect of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ἐγκεφάλου ἐσακούσαντος τοῦ
					τρώματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Prorrh.</u>
					2.14
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			 in strict sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔξωθεν εἰς τὰς οἰκίας εἰσακούεται
					μᾶλλον ἢ ἔσωθεν ἔξω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					903b13
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴσω ἀκ.</span>
			).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
